            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CARRIE HUBBARD"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The cookies turned out good. They don’t taste like sugar cookies though, more like shortbread. My chocolate chips started to cool before I got all the cookies dipped and then the cookie would break when I tried to pull it out f the chocolate. I would suggest adding something like butter to the chocolate chips to thin it out."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is excellent! I got a lot of compliments. I used a cookie press and they looked like store-bought cookies. Caution if you use a press add flour. A pastry brush helps apply the chocolate. This recipe is quick and easy.",
            "datePublished": "2001-11-19T06:29:52.310Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CurvyPea7793"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Poor recipe for two main reasons. 1. No salt - a key ingredient in any sweet, bringing out all the flavors more brightly. Cookies without salt are flat and dimensionless. And 2. Egg whites - no instruction to beat or otherwise prepare before adding, implying one should add egg whites as is. But any other recipe would specify to beat the whites to a fluffy consistency before adding (as in a meringue), to trap air and give the characteristic lightness to the cookies. Omitting this step is not an option, just an an oversight.",
            "datePublished": "2024-02-04T20:30:46.405Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ok"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made a few changes that worked out nicely, I added 1/3 cup of white sugar and brown sugar (lightly packed) and used 10 tbsp of butter, I also used 1 cup of flour instead, the cookies spread out more and were a lot more crisp with this ratio, its also a little less chalky.",
            "datePublished": "2019-05-12T17:46:31.780Z"
          },
          {
